    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s just weird because people always say \"it gets better\" or \"there's always something to look forward to\" but that feels like such a lie. it’s just more chores, more noise. if the universe is as indifferent as it looks, then why is there this massive social pressure to keep dragging ourselves through it? why is staying alive considered a \"duty\" when it’s really just a biological reflex?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
